  "notes": "Cash-basis county audit, FYE 6/30/2022. Page 1 is the auditor's report page on supplementary information (no figures). Statement lines from the Total Governmental Funds column of the Statement of Cash Receipts, Disbursements, and Changes in Cash Basis Fund Balance (p5). The p5 major column headed 'Federal Disaster Grant Fund' is the ARPA Fund (same 572,614 ending balance as the p4 ARPA Fund column and the p8 ARPA schedule); the nonmajor Federal Disaster Grants fund is a separate column on p9. 'Taxes' 5,929,864: the Statement of Activities (p3) prints no tax-type breakdown; the Inheritance Fund's 724,333 is inheritance tax by fund name and the General Fund 5,030,273 + Building Fund 175,258 stay taxes (unlabeled). Beginning cash not printed (null); beginning/ending fund balance from p5; ending cash = printed Cash and cash equivalents 6,119,948 (p4). Balance sheet from the governmental funds Statement of Cash Basis Assets and Fund Balances (p4), whose totals equal the Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p2: restricted by purpose 301,854 + unrestricted 5,818,094; its classification differs from the fund statement's restricted 402,829). Statement of Activities change in net position 1,421,251 ties to the fund statement. Transfers: General out 1,387,197 to Road; nonmajor 911 System Fund (6,033) to E-911 Sheriff Funds 6,033 (netted to zero in the nonmajor total). Detail: General Fund budget schedule (p6), major fund budget schedules for Road, Inheritance, Building, ARPA (pp7-8), and nonmajor per-fund budget schedules (pp10-14; STOP Program schedule = Pretrial Diversion column of the p9 combining statement); the p9 combining statement is used only for disbursement functions, so it is not double counted. Lines with zero actual and zero budget skipped; Juvenile Diversion disbursements (actual 0, budget 2,398) skipped since no function is printed for it. Read pages 1-14 of 14"
